WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.900
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:11.020
JOY PAYTON: I've had people
come to me at work or just

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:15.350
in the community and say, hey,
I saw in LinkedIn that you

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:16.840
were Google Cloud certified.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:19.150
I want to find out
more about this.

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:21.610
And these are often
career changers,

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:24.440
or people who discovered,
to their surprise,

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:28.840
that they really liked devops,
or platform engineering,

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:32.409
or some of the
background engineering.

00:00:32.409 --> 00:00:35.170
And maybe that wasn't the
job that they were hired for,

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:38.560
but they realized that, wow,
I have some technical skills

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:41.540
and abilities that
I didn't know about.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:44.800
And in fact, I had a
conversation with someone

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:49.120
who has a lot of information
science experience

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:51.100
but is not a programmer.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:54.280
She would not consider
herself a programmer.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:55.690
And she said, can I pursue this?

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:58.540
I said, absolutely.

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:02.710
There are specialty
professional-grade exams

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:10.360
for applications developers,
but this initial associate-level

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:14.237
exam is just a great overview
of lots of different things.

00:01:14.237 --> 00:01:16.570
And I said, if nothing else,
what it will do is give you

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:19.930
a chance to learn a lot,
figure out what parts you like

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:22.170
and what parts you don't.

